# Implementation Plan: Deploy Website via Cloudflare Tunnel

This plan outlines the steps to make your local **UniServerZ** website accessible over the internet using a **Cloudflare Tunnel**. This is the most secure and easiest method as it avoids port forwarding.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Temporary vs. Permanent URL:**
> - By default, this plan starts with a **Quick Tunnel** (`*.trycloudflare.com`). This provides a temporary link that works as long as the tunnel is running.
> - For a **Permanent URL** (e.g., `www.yourshop.com`), you will eventually need a registered domain name and a free Cloudflare account.

> [!WARNING]
> **Server Uptime:**
> Your website will only be accessible while your PC is on and both UniServerZ and the tunnel program are running.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Download Cloudflare Tunnel Tools
I will download the official `cloudflared.exe` binary to your `f:\UniServerZ` folder. This tool is the "bridge" between your PC and the Cloudflare network.

### 2. Verify Local Server Port
Based on your logs, the server appears to be running on **Port 81** (`localhost:81`). I will confirm this is active before starting the tunnel.

### 3. Launch the Tunnel
I will run a command to generate a public link for you.
- **Command:** `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:81`
- **Result:** You will receive a unique link (like `random-name.trycloudflare.com`) that anyone can use to visit your site.

### 4. Setup for "Always On" (Optional)
If you want the site to stay up permanently, I can show you how to:
- Move the tunnel configuration to a "Service" so it starts with your PC.
- (If you have a domain) Point your domain to this tunnel.

## Open Questions

1. **Do you already have a domain name** (e.g., `.com`, `.net`) or a Cloudflare account?
2. **Is Port 81 the correct port** for your shop? (I can verify this once we start).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I'll use the browser tool to ping the local server `http://localhost:81/coolex_shop` to ensure it's up.
- After starting the tunnel, I'll use the browser tool to visit the generated `*.trycloudflare.com` link.

### Manual Verification
- You will be able to visit the link on your mobile phone or another device to confirm it works globally.
